{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Sir, just to tell you, he reached twenty minutes late. I almost gave the slot away.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Sorry doctor, really sorry. The metro was stuck and then parking itself took so long, I went round and round. I told madam please don't cancel.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (DOCTOR): Right. Sit. What is the problem?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Actually the reason I came, since four days I am having burning when I pass urine, and I am going to the toilet again and again. That is worrying me.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (DOCTOR): Four days?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, from Monday night. I finished one long call, went to pass urine, and uh the burning started. I thought it is the office AC only, I hardly drink water when I am in meetings.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any discharge?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): No sir. No discharge. I checked the underwear also, no stain, nothing sticky, nothing at all.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (DOCTOR): Fever?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No fever.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (DOCTOR): Back pain?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm, yes. There is a lower back ache, both sides, dull only, not the sharp stone type pain. It is there since the same four days. If I bend to pick up the laptop bag it pulls a little more.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): Travelled recently?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No no, I have not travelled. Only house to office and back. No outstation, no function, nothing like that.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): How many times are you passing urine?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): On normal days five or six times. Now it is almost every hour, and each time only a little comes. At night I got up two times, last night three times. The burning is sharp, the whole stream, and if I hold the urine in a meeting it becomes worse.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Doctor, vitals. Temperature 37.8 celsius, pulse 92, BP 130 over 84, oxygen 98 percent.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (DOCTOR): You said no fever. It is 37.8.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): Ah, sorry sir, I forgot. Last night I was feeling hot, a little bit of fever only. My wife checked, it was 99 point something, I took one crocine and felt a bit better, so in the morning I said no fever. It is mild, not a high fever.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (DOCTOR): Blood in the urine?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): No blood sir. I was checking every time because I got scared it might be blood. The colour is yellow, a bit dark, but not red.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (DOCTOR): Vomiting? Stomach pain?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): No vomiting. No pain in the stomach as such. Only the lower back I already said. Motions are normal, once a day, no loose motion, though you did not ask, I am just telling.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): Diabetes?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): No sir, no diabetes. Last year in the company check the fasting sugar was normal, some ninety something. BP I have, since about five years. Every morning I take amlong 5 mg, that small white BP tablet, after brushing, and I don't miss it.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): Drug allergy?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): No, no allergy to any medicine. I have taken penicillin before, for a tooth, and crocine so many times. No rash, no swelling, nothing.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't smoke. Alcohol, sometimes one beer on a weekend, not even every week. I am in software, sitting the whole day, err, exercise is very less, I should walk more.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (DOCTOR): Stay still. No loin tenderness. Abdomen is soft.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): Burning, frequency, and this temperature. Most likely a urine infection, I am not confirming it. Urine routine and culture today. Antibiotic only if the report shows infection.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): I will give the container now and send the sample to the lab today itself.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): Drink two and a half to three litres of water. Do not stop the amlong. Come back in three days with the report. If the pain gets severe or the fever shoots up, come earlier.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Ok sir, I will come. I forget water in meetings, I will keep a bottle on the desk itself. My neighbour said cranberry juice and I bought one bottle, should I drink that?",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (DOCTOR): No. Plain water is enough. Three days."
 ],
